# K03 NS-ROLES-1b (Codex K03-NS-ROLES-NEXT-20261007-09; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md:666, :668): after `box: Model` the
# application of box is Model's -- `box()` and the bare `box` run Model's body as `Model()` does (an argument is
# refused: an ordinary named Structure takes none); nothing runs at the binding.
# In a method.  Exit 7; 81 if the binding ran Model, 82 if box() and box did not each run it once.
int: hits 0
Model:
    int: v 1
    node\hits: node\hits + 1
end: Model
fn: m () int
    box: Model
    if: node\hits != 0
        return: 81
    box()
    box
    if: node\hits != 2
        return: 82
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
